C EXAMPLES FOR MCP write_file + cc + as

Workflow for each example:
  write_file('/tmp/demo.c', CONTENT)
  cc /tmp/demo.c
  as /tmp/demo.s
  /tmp/a.out
Use separate calls, inspect errors. The output is overwritten.

1. Hello stdout (string literal form supported by cc)
  int main() {
      write(1, "Hello\n", 6);
      return 0;
  }
Expected: Hello

2. Loop and signed comparisons
  int main() {
      int i = 0;
      while (i < 3) {
          write(1, "*", 1);
          i = i + 1;
      }
      write(1, "\n", 1);
      return 0;
  }
Expected: ***

3. Local pointer and function call
  void set(int *p) {
      *p = 65;
      return;
  }
  int main() {
      int a = 0;
      char b[2] = "X";
      set(&a);
      if (a == 65) {
          write(1, b, 1);
      }
      return 0;
  }
Expected: X

Limitations: no printf; no standard #include; no global variables;
no for loop; comparisons in if/while; <=1024 B total C source.
A successful cc only writes .s: you MUST still run as. The final
binary is always /tmp/a.out. Program may fault on bad pointers.
